            },
            {
              "name": "pkic:profile:integrationConstraints",
              "value": "Keys are held in TR-31 key blocks protected by AES-256 main keys in the service's HSMs, which meet the PCI PTS HSM requirements (foundations page). A key exists in a single AWS Region (terminology page). A customer can import its own keys, but the service always holds them under its own main keys, so custody is provider-managed."
